<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grobogan Regency</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grobogan is a regency in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-java">Central Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semarang">Semarang</a>, with its seat at Purwodadi. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultivation-system">Cultivation System</a> it was struck by a severe famine in 1849–1850, when crop failures combined with the burdens of forced cultivation killed many thousands of people. With the earlier famine in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirebon">Cirebon</a>, the disaster gave critics of the colonial system evidence of its human cost.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grobogan-regency.jpg" alt="Grobogan Regency" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PL09Puryono · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tugu_selamat_datang_Purwodadi_JATENG.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
